                         |CKBChapter 7 - Equipment
                     |BKB-----------------------------------

|YKOCharacters can wear equipment on the head, body, legs, hands, feet,
shield arm, cloak/body, shoulders, aura, two fingers, and two neck slots.
Weapons occupy your hands according to their own rules. Race, size, guild,
class, strength, curses, and scripted restrictions can all affect what fits.

Use:

  |YKBeq|YKO or |YKBmyeq|YKO           Review equipped items
  |YKBequip <item>|YKO                 Equip an item in an appropriate slot
  |YKBwear <item>|YKO                  Wear armour
  |YKBwield <item>|YKO                 Wield a weapon
  |YKBgearcheck|YKO                    Compare carried and equipped gear
  |YKBgearcheck <item>|YKO             Inspect one detailed comparison
  |YKBloadout|YKO                      Manage named equipment presets

|YKBset itemdetail on|YKO adds raw weapon and armour ratings to item
descriptions. Gearcheck considers protection, weapon class, stats,
resistances, durability, known effects, and the slots an item would replace.
Its result is advice; sidegrades can still suit a particular build.

Equipment may also have an item level. This describes where it belongs in
game progression and how ranked weapons and armour interact; it is not by
itself a minimum character level. Read separately listed restrictions.

Qualifying carried, worn, and wielded gear saves when you leave. Donated,
broken, unique, consumable, non-droppable, and specially restricted gear may
not save. Items inside containers do not save merely because the container
does, and temporary equipment modifications are stripped on return.

With a corpse burner carried, |YKBset autosell on|YKO transmits ordinary
sellable NPC loot to Taylor.
|YKBset autorefine on|YKO converts eligible ordinary NPC equipment into
profession materials. They are mutually exclusive, and both permanently
process items before autoloot, so leave them off while learning what drops.|000

